  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 208 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nBy Wednesday morning, an upper level disturbance will translate to \nthe east across the Great Plains and a cold front will move through \nthe region. The passage of this weak front and upper level ridging \nbuilding in across the Rockies will provide for drier conditions \nareawide through the middle of the week. During that time, daytime \nhighs reach into the upper 60s to low 70s and lows settle into the \n40s for most, which will be near normal for nearly mid-November. \nLong range guidance/ensembles continue to suggest an upper low \nmoving in from the Pacific and crossing northern Mexico before \nmaking it to West Texas. However, plenty of uncertainty exists with \njust where this low will track and how that might influence rain \nchances in the region. \n\n-Stickney",
